0 Fixture: two 43038 quarter racks lap-joined into a half circle, with a
0 beam right behind the joint. Expected: clean.
0
0 24121.dat (kit 43038) is full thickness except its two end tabs, which
0 are half thickness on one face: local y 0..10 only. Two quarters meet in
0 ONE plane, one of them turned half a turn about the vertical, so the two
0 tabs land on opposite faces and stack into one full-thickness lug. That
0 is how four of them close a circle. An axle through the lug locks both.
0
0 The end-tab bore is drawn as axlehol4 scaled 0 10 0. The checker used to
0 read every one-sided axle hole as a full module deep, so the left tab's
0 bore ran 10 LDU out of the plastic into the 13M beam behind it and the
0 axle reported PIN SLICE CONFLICT on a joint that is fine. A one-sided
0 axle hole drawn half a module deep is now read at its drawn depth.
0
0 The 9M upright ties the two 13M beams together so every part has two
0 non-collinear connections and nothing here is a hinge. The tabs are
0 each half a module, so SHALLOW ENGAGEMENT warns, which is the truth.
